First details on the new circuits, new cars, Family Mode, and more coming in 2026.
Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV update launching in two parts later this year
As we look ahead to the 30 th anniversary of the original release of Gran Turismo in 2027, we are preparing a free Spec IV update for Gran Turismo 7 to kick off the celebrations with our players. Due to the number of updates coming in Spec IV, it will be released in two parts, with the first arriving in October and the second in December.
Across these two updates, players can look forward to new circuits&nbsp;and&nbsp;cars,&nbsp;additional&nbsp;ways to compete, and features designed to make the world of Gran Turismo more welcoming and enjoyable for everyone.&nbsp;
The second is Autumn Ring, a circuit deeply connected to the&nbsp;history&nbsp;of Gran Turismo, first appearing in the original title. I am very pleased&nbsp;to&nbsp;bring this circuit into Gran Turismo 7 as part of the December release and allow millions of players to experience it for the first time.
A total of 12 cars will be added&nbsp;across both Spec IV updates. The exact cars will be revealed at a later time.&nbsp;
Spec IV will also introduce a selection of new game features and even&nbsp;offer&nbsp;more ways for players to find their own challenge.&nbsp;
Together, these additions are designed to offer new goals for experienced drivers while creating more opportunities for every player to explore Gran Turismo 7 on their own terms.&nbsp;
Family Mode will be included in the December update. Family Mode is a new way to make Gran Turismo 7 more accessible and enjoyable when playing with family and friends.&nbsp;
A new circuit and the return of a&nbsp;legacy circuit &nbsp;

New gameplay debuts, Premium Editions and pre-order bonuses revealed.
Final Fantasy VII Revelation launches on PS5 April 8, 2027
During today&#8217;s PlayStation State of Play broadcast, we revealed substantial new gameplay footage for Final Fantasy VII Revelation , and confirmed that the game will launch for PlayStation 5 on April 8, 2027.
The&nbsp;anticipated&nbsp;action RPG&nbsp;will be&nbsp;the final entry in the acclaimed&nbsp;Final Fantasy VII&nbsp;Remake&nbsp;Series,&nbsp;delivering the epic&nbsp;finale&nbsp;to the story that began in&nbsp;Final Fantasy VII&nbsp;Remake&nbsp;and continued in&nbsp;Final Fantasy VII&nbsp;Rebirth.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Set in a vast open world realized on an unprecedented scale,&nbsp;Final Fantasy VII Revelation&nbsp;gives players&nbsp;new&nbsp;opportunities&nbsp;to explore the planet via the iconic&nbsp;Highwind&nbsp;airship.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Final Fantasy VII Revelation&nbsp;will&nbsp;introduce a new dynamic character-switching feature that allows players to instantly swap between party members while exploring the world.&nbsp;Traversal has also been upgraded through the addition of a grappling gun that will allow players to quickly scale rooftops and navigate the city with style.&nbsp;
For card game lovers, fan-favorite minigame Queen&#8217;s Blood makes a return in Final Fantasy VII Revelation &#8212; this time with a major new storyline centered on Red XIII. Players will face powerful new opponents and unique gameplay challenges that expand upon the strategic card&nbsp;game&#8217;s&nbsp;mechanics. The new Queen&#8217;s Blood campaign introduces opponents capable of dramatically altering the flow of matches, creating fresh challenges for even experienced players.&nbsp;
Pre-orders are live on PlayStation Store today. A&nbsp;special pre-order&nbsp;bonus is available for all editions of Final Fantasy VII Revelation: fans&nbsp;who pre-order the game will receive the Mecha-Chocobo&nbsp;&#038;&nbsp;Moogle&nbsp;Summon Materia.&nbsp;
There&#8217;s&nbsp;also&nbsp;a Final Fantasy VII Revelation&nbsp;Premium Edition, which includes&nbsp;the main game, Story Expansion Pass, and Early Access, which&nbsp;will&nbsp;allow for&nbsp;access to the game&nbsp;24 hours before its release.&nbsp;The Premium Edition will also include an in-game accessory&nbsp;(Reclaimant Choker), as well as a set of consumable items to support the&nbsp;early stages&nbsp;of the journey.&nbsp;As its title suggests, the Story Expansion Pass will grant access to two story-centered&nbsp;DLC, with more exciting details on these to come at a later point!

News on over 30 games across two packed shows.
State of Play & State of Play Japan: all announcements, trailers
Two shows, over 30 games. Today’s double-sized State of Play brings together creatives from the world over to debut new games, share deep gameplay dives and fresh insights, reveal release dates, and much more. We’ve wrapped up every single announcement into this recap, handily organised in alphabetical order. Watch the trailers, get up to speed on the reveals, and for a select number of games, you can enjoy further information directly from the developers behind them in a series of exclusive PlayStation Blog articles.&nbsp;
State of Play &#038; State of Play Japan
CONQ: Crown of No Quarter was revealed with its first trailer, introducing a new warfare experience set in a shared open world. Players can lead armies across land and sea, storm enemy strongholds, build siege engines, and fight for their faction in large-scale battles.&nbsp;
The massive action adventure from Pearl Abyss is getting even larger with Charting the Unknown, a mammoth expansion arriving on PlayStation Store October 15. The above trailer, captured on PS5 Pro, gives you a taste of the rich gameplay variety that awaits as Kliff, Oongka, and Damiane set out to discover their purpose and shape their futures.&nbsp;
Daba: Land of Water Scar, developed by Dark Star Games as part of PlayStation’s China Hero Project, is coming to PS5 in Spring 2027. A new trailer gives us another look at its fantastical world, where players take on the role of a clayman journeying across a land where the waters have run dry.&nbsp;
Dragon Ball Xenoverse 3 comes to PS5 in 2027. Today’s State of Play trailer offers a look at this new Dragon Ball adventure, where players can create their own hero, develop their own fighting style, and take on powerful opponents.&nbsp;
Genesis Maiden, the first DLC for Sword Art Online: Echoes of Aincrad, arrives this winter. The expansion features a new story set on the early floors of Aincrad, with Mito joining the fight alongside new gameplay additions.&nbsp;
